def select_competitor(self, population):
    elitism_count = min(len(population) // 10, 5)
    elite_pool = population[:elitism_count]
    remaining = population[elitism_count:]

    tournament_size = 5
    elite_tournaments = [self._tournament_selection(tournament) for _ in range(tournament_size) for tournament in elite_pool]

    exploration_pool = random.sample(remaining, len(population) - elitism_count)
    exploration_tournaments = [self._tournament_selection(tournament) for tournament in exploration_pool]

    all_tournaments = elite_tournaments + exploration_tournaments

    return max(all_tournaments, key=lambda x: x['fitness'] if x['fitness'] is not None else -1)
```

In this implementation, I have added elitism by taking the top 5% of the population as elites, while the rest are used for exploration. I have also used a tournament selection mechanism with a tournament size of 5, which allows for a balance between elitism and exploration. This should help the GA to explore the search space more aggressively and break out of local minima.
